WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.700
Dictionaries.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.933
Every API response, model config, and tool call you meet as an AI engineer arrives as a dictionary.

3
00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:15.500
A dictionary maps keys to values, and looking one up is fast, constant time on average.

4
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:20.333
Keys must be hashable, so strings, numbers, and tuples work, but lists don't.

5
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:24.900
Since Python three seven, dictionaries also remember insertion order.

6
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.667
Why is lookup so fast?

7
00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:29.033
You give it a key.

8
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.267
Python hashes the key into a number.

9
00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.467
That number points straight to one slot.

10
00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.661
And the value is sitting right there.

11
00:00:35.661 --> 00:00:36.633
Nothing is scanned.

12
00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:41.533
Real JSON is dictionaries nested inside dictionaries.

13
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:44.533
The top object has a name and a hazard flag.

14
00:00:44.833 --> 00:00:46.833
And a nested diameter dictionary.

15
00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:50.433
To reach the number, you just chain the keys, level by level.

16
00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:53.200
Here are the habits that matter.

17
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.233
Dot get with a default survives a missing key instead of crashing.

18
00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:02.433
A dict comprehension reshapes a list of records into a name to size map.

19
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:06.300
And dot items lets you loop over keys and values together.

20
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.500
Four tools cover most daily work.

21
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.233
Get with a default, for inconsistent data.

22
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:13.833
Items, for looping.

23
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:16.067
Comprehensions, for reshaping.

24
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.333
And the pipe operator, which merges two dictionaries.

25
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:22.133
Here's where this keeps you safe.

26
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:26.733
The DONKI service returns flare entries where some fields are simply missing.

27
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:30.433
Chained gets with defaults keep your agent's tool from crashing.

28
00:01:30.733 --> 00:01:37.233
And the arguments an LLM sends to a tool are a dictionary too, so the same discipline validates them.

29
00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:39.172
Let's recap.

30
00:01:39.172 --> 00:01:42.433
A dictionary is a hash map with constant time lookup.

31
00:01:42.733 --> 00:01:44.800
All JSON becomes a dictionary.

32
00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.867
Use get defaults, items, and comprehensions.

33
00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:50.452
And remember keys must be hashable.

34
00:01:50.452 --> 00:01:51.367
Next up: sets.
